-- TS - AI Ideas Hub — Core Competency, P3-P5 (Specialist / Senior / Principal) seed
--
-- Adds the Specialist (P3), Senior Specialist (P4), and Principal Specialist
-- (P5) tiers of Skedulo TS's career ladder to the existing Core Competency
-- track — the rest of the ladder above Junior (P2), which
-- junior-learning-roadmap-seed.sql already covers. Source: "TS Career Track
-- - Learning Plan Master.xlsx", the same 12 competency tabs as before,
-- importing every row marked Level = 'Intermediate' (-> 'middle') or
-- 'Advanced' (-> 'senior' or 'principal', disambiguated by that row's own
-- Role column — see below). Quiz questions come from "Quizzes - Specialist +
-- Senior + Principal.xlsx", matched to courses positionally: both files are
-- built from the exact same tab-by-tab, row-by-row traversal of the source
-- roadmap, so the Nth quiz sheet always corresponds to the Nth course row
-- extracted the same way — confirmed by comparing every one of the 56 pairs'
-- own title text before relying on it, not assumed.
--
-- Not a new track: same Core Competency track row as every other Core
-- Competency seed file. No `tracks` insert here. Explicitly does NOT touch
-- the Intern (P1) or Junior (P2) tiers already seeded by
-- core-competency-seed.sql and junior-learning-roadmap-seed.sql — this file
-- only ever INSERTs new courses (ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING) and, for those new
-- courses only, sets skills and quiz content. It carries no reconciliation
-- logic against either of those two files.
--
-- Level/Role mismatch: the source lists the Troubleshooting tab's
-- "...Webhooks and Triggered Actions..." row under Level = 'Intermediate',
-- but that row's own Role column says 'Senior Specialist', and the quiz
-- workbook's own tab for it independently agrees ("Level: Advanced — Senior
-- Specialist"). Role is the more specific, unambiguous signal (it maps 1:1
-- to intern/junior/middle/senior/principal; Level is a coarser display
-- bucket), so every course below is tiered from its own Role column, not
-- the Level column — this is the one row where the two disagree.
--
-- 56 raw 'Intermediate'/'Advanced' rows across the 12 tabs, 55 land here as
-- courses. 'Crisis Communication: Essential Skills for Crisis Management'
-- (Incident Mgmt & Escalation) is listed twice — once at Specialist, once
-- at Senior Specialist, same title, same link, two different 10-question
-- quiz banks (source tabs IE-05 and IE-07). courses' natural key is
-- (track_id, title), so it can only be one row: kept at its lower tier
-- (middle), with the higher-tier IE-07 quiz bank folded in as positions
-- 11-20 on that same course rather than dropped — this is the one course
-- in this file with 20 quiz questions instead of 10.
--
-- Of those 55, 2 titles ('Mastering Collaboration: Work together for the
-- best results', 'TED — Dan Pink: The puzzle of motivation') are already
-- seeded at the Intern tier by core-competency-seed.sql — the source lists
-- them again as still-relevant reading at Specialist. ON CONFLICT DO
-- NOTHING leaves the existing Intern-tier row exactly as it is (per this
-- file's own scope above, Intern/Junior are untouched), so these two
-- simply don't gain a second row here.
--
-- 6 courses had only a "Search on Free - Udemy (org subscription) — no
-- direct URL provided" placeholder for a link in the roadmap sheet
-- (Leading Technical Teams, Advanced Excel/Google Sheets, KPI Reporting,
-- Advanced Dashboard & Reporting Design, Strategic Account Management and
-- Contract Negotiation, Training Program Design for Adult Learners) — each
-- one's own quiz tab independently names a real Udemy URL as its source, so
-- that real URL is used for `link` below instead of the placeholder text.
--
-- Skills reuse Core Competency's existing 8-skill taxonomy
-- (core-competency-seed.sql) — no new skill needed for any of the 55.
--
-- roadmap_order continues the sequence junior-learning-roadmap-seed.sql
-- left off at (that file used 37-48): 49-103 here, in the same
-- tab-then-row order as the source.
--
-- Not destructive to run — every insert here is ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING,
-- safe to re-run on a database that already has some or all of this
-- content; nothing here is a DELETE or an UPDATE against an existing row,
-- so re-running this file can never touch a real learner's
-- course_assignments or an existing course_quiz_questions row.
--
-- Run schema.sql and core-competency-seed.sql first (this depends on the
-- Core Competency track already existing).

-- 55 real resources — see file header for the 1 duplicate title folded in
-- and the 2 that already exist at the Intern tier.
insert into courses (track_id, stage, focus_area, title, platform, priority, est_hours, cost, outcome, expected_by_position, link, roadmap_order)
select (select id from tracks where name = 'Core Competency'), v.*
from (values
  ('L2 — Intermediate', 'Troubleshooting', 'Debugging Tools and Techniques for the Lightning Platform', 'Salesforce Trailhead', 'core', 0.25, 'Free', 'Reads an Apex debug log to pinpoint where a customisation is failing, without waiting on engineering.', 'middle', 'https://trailhead.salesforce.com/content/learn/modules/apex_basics_dotnet/debugging_diagnostics', 49),
  ('L2 — Intermediate', 'Troubleshooting', 'Skedulo Developer Guide — API Overview & REST API reference', 'developer.skedulo.com', 'core', 2.0, 'Free (internal)', 'Diagnoses whether a customer-reported fault sits in the core API or a customisation, using the API reference directly.', 'middle', 'https://developer.skedulo.com/developer-guides/integration-and-automation/api-overview/', 50),
  ('L3 — Advanced', 'Troubleshooting', 'Skedulo Developer Guide — Webhooks and Triggered Actions (overview + create a webhook)', 'developer.skedulo.com', 'core', 2.0, 'Free (internal)', 'Coordinates with cross-functional teams on an integration-level defect using expert-level knowledge of Skedulo''s event/webhook model.', 'senior', 'https://developer.skedulo.com/developer-guides/integration-and-automation/webhooks-and-triggered-actions/overview-webhooks-and-triggered-actions/', 51),
